I chant my nation's crucial stage, (America's, haply humani-
ty'shumanity's
)—the trial great, the victory great,

The scout call'd up and forward—the General
mounted and his aids around him—the new
brought word—the instantaneous order issued;

The clank of cavalry—the strange celerity of form-
ingforming
ranks— the slender bugle note;

Out spake pleas'd NATURE, (the round impassive Globe,
with all its shows of Day and Night,) saying,
He is mine;
